prompt.text:
Implement a new TypeScript module for transforming an in-memory voxel palette, using no external packages:

```ts
export interface RGB { readonly r: number; readonly g: number; readonly b: number; }
export interface VoxelGrid {
  readonly width: number;
  readonly height: number;
  readonly depth: number;
  readonly colors: readonly RGB[];
}
export interface Grade {
  readonly gain: RGB;
  readonly offset: RGB;
}
export function gradeVoxels(grid: VoxelGrid, grade: Grade): VoxelGrid;
```

Dimensions must be nonnegative integers. The color count must equal `width * height * depth`; mismatches throw `RangeError`, including nonempty colors for any zero-volume grid. Every color, gain, and offset channel must be finite or `RangeError` is thrown. For each channel compute `input * gain + offset`, then clamp to `[0,255]` and round to the nearest integer using `Math.round`. Preserve the flat color ordering. Return a new grid, new color array, and new color objects, even for an empty grid. Do not mutate or alias any input object or array. Reject products that are not safe integers with `RangeError`.

